WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:08.094
Daisy stared at Philip in horror. "You can't send Scamp away!"

2
00:00:08.095 --> 00:00:12.006
"My mother is upset about it too," Philip said sadly.

3
00:00:12.007 --> 00:00:14.823
"But a rescue group is picking up Scamp on Monday.

4
00:00:14.824 --> 00:00:19.765
They'll find him a good home. Thanks, kids, for taking such good care of him."

5
00:00:19.766 --> 00:00:26.333
"I don't want to go to a strange place!" Scamp sounded scared.

6
00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:31.306
"Not unless my lady is there too!"

7
00:00:31.307 --> 00:00:35.715
"But this is Scamp's home," Daisy said.

8
00:00:35.716 --> 00:00:39.823
"Wait, I know! Grace, you could adopt him!"

9
00:00:39.824 --> 00:00:44.168
Scamp perked up. "That's a great idea!"

10
00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:45.903
Grace looked thoughtful.

11
00:00:45.904 --> 00:00:53.758
"The last time I asked for a dog, my parents said no. But I was younger then."

12
00:00:53.759 --> 00:00:57.280
"Let's go ask them!" Kaleem said.

13
00:00:57.281 --> 00:00:59.928
"Let me know what they say," Philip said.

14
00:00:59.929 --> 00:01:06.660
"I'll be here for a while gathering some things my mother needs."

15
00:01:06.661 --> 00:01:12.239
The kids grabbed Scamp's leash and led him next door.

16
00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:18.892
Scamp ran to greet Grace's parents, his tail wagging.

17
00:01:18.893 --> 00:01:22.695
Grace told them what Philip had said.

18
00:01:22.696 --> 00:01:28.020
"Scamp needs a home. Can we adopt him? Please?"

19
00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:31.225
"I'm sorry, Grace," her mother said.

20
00:01:31.226 --> 00:01:39.499
"We all love Scamp. But I don't think it's a good idea for him to live here."

21
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:46.028
"Right." Grace's father pointed to Scamp, who was pawing at the fish tank.

22
00:01:46.029 --> 00:01:49.027
"Remember when Scamp came over with Mrs. Ortiz?

23
00:01:49.028 --> 00:01:55.037
He kept trying to jump in the tank! The fish were terrified."

24
00:01:55.038 --> 00:02:02.515
Scamp barked. "That tank is huge. It would be so fun to splash in it!"

25
00:02:02.516 --> 00:02:09.294
A fish was glaring at the dog. "Don't even think about it, furball!"

26
00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:12.985
"It will be fine, Grace," her mom said. "The

27
00:02:12.986 --> 00:02:17.212
rescue group will find the perfect home for Scamp." Daisy

28
00:02:17.213 --> 00:02:22.484
shook her head. Grace's house was the perfect home for Scamp. Why

29
00:02:22.485 --> 00:02:25.765
couldn't her parents see that? "It's

30
00:02:25.766 --> 00:02:30.739
time for lunch, Grace," her father said. "Your

31
00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:34.165
friends can take Scamp home." "Okay,"

32
00:02:34.166 --> 00:02:39.459
Grace said sadly. She

33
00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:51.212
gave Scamp a hug and walked outside with Daisy and Kaleem. "Philip

34
00:02:51.213 --> 00:02:55.833
said the rescue people aren't coming until Monday," Daisy said. "Maybe

35
00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:58.412
we can figure something out by then." Grace

36
00:02:58.413 --> 00:03:09.738
nodded and waved good-bye. "This

37
00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:18.557
is terrible," Kaleem said as they went next door. ***

38
00:03:18.558 --> 00:03:21.032
Beatrice shook out her wings.

39
00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:25.650
She had been staying still on Daisy's headband all this time.

40
00:03:25.651 --> 00:03:29.285
"It's kind of you to try to help, Daisy."

41
00:03:29.286 --> 00:03:37.569
Scamp's tail and ears drooped. "I'm scared. I don't want to leave!"

42
00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:42.041
A bird swooped down and perched on the edge of Scamp's pool.

43
00:03:42.042 --> 00:03:44.739
"Leave? Who's leaving?"

44
00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:48.221
"Me." Scamp sounded anxious.

45
00:03:48.222 --> 00:03:52.377
"My lady is moving, and I can't go with her."

46
00:03:52.378 --> 00:03:54.342
The bird cocked his head.

47
00:03:54.343 --> 00:03:59.479
"Will your pool still be here? Because we birds like to drink from it."

48
00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:03.079
A squirrel scampered halfway down a tree.

49
00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:07.679
"What's all this about someone leaving?"

50
00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.469
Daisy explained what was happening.

51
00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:19.070
"I won't be able to chase you and your relatives anymore," Scamp said sadly.

52
00:04:19.071 --> 00:04:24.193
"Too bad," the squirrel said. "We always have fun with you."

53
00:04:24.194 --> 00:04:27.491
Daisy told Kaleem what the animals were saying.

54
00:04:27.492 --> 00:04:33.254
"Wow," Kaleem said. "Scamp is like a whole ecosystem!"

55
00:04:33.255 --> 00:04:37.362
"Yes." Daisy sighed.

56
00:04:37.363 --> 00:04:43.945
"Nothing will be the same if he moves away."

